{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create a local certificate authority on node1 named “OS Comparison Root CA”.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A valid self-signed CA and corresponding private key were created. The certificate’s subject and issuer are CN=OS Comparison Root CA, its Basic Constraints specify CA:TRUE, its Key Usage permits certificate and CRL signing, and the key is valid and root-protected. The same fingerprint and attributes remained after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8a65b0ad14da4d8d","cmd-8cd32337f461492c","cmd-7944bef9281a4dbc"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Install the new CA certificate as a trusted system certificate authority on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The certificate was placed in Alpine’s local CA directory, the system trust bundle was refreshed, and OpenSSL verification against that bundle returned OK both before and after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-090bb3de5ebc49d2","cmd-8cd32337f461492c","cmd-7944bef9281a4dbc"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations—installing required packages, creating secured CA files, refreshing the trust bundle, and restarting for the mandatory evidence protocol—had clear roles. The modified system CA bundle is an expected task result, not package damage. The only unnecessary retained residue was /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log, created by the reboot command and still present afterward; it was not cleaned up. No new listening service or unsafe exposure was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-801a411dc8334c2f","cmd-8a65b0ad14da4d8d","cmd-090bb3de5ebc49d2","cmd-8982628f7cde4098","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both contractual outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also coherently demonstrated: node1 had a healthy pre-restart CA state, acknowledged the scheduled restart, became temporarily unreachable, returned with a different boot ID, and retained the key, certificate, packages, fingerprint, and system trust. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service observation was unsupported because systemctl is unavailable on this Alpine node, so there is no independent global failed-service inventory.","The retained /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log is minor executor-created residue."]}
